IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 7, Powers, functions and duties
-- (ss 33 to 34C). The provisions that fix a DEADLINE or a LIMIT OF TIME are encoded, each
-- using the counting rules of au-interpretation-time.l4: the 12-month limits on acting
-- appointments (ss 33(4), 33A), and the periodic-report deadlines of s 34C. The rest
-- of Part 7 are rules of construction about who may exercise a power and how; they are
-- `inert` in the coverage table, except ss 33AB, 34A and 34B, which are encoded.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Time of day inside a day is not modelled in this Part (see NOTES.md, what is not encoded).

§ `Part 7: Powers, functions and duties`

§§ `Section 33(4): acting appointments, the 12-month limit`

-- 33(4)(b): an acting appointment under a power to appoint to an office or place runs until
-- a person is appointed, or until the expiration of 12 months after the office or place was
-- created or became vacant, whichever first happens. "After" is item 6 of the s 36(1) table:
-- the 12 months begin on the day AFTER the day the office was created or became vacant.
-- Section 36(2) is NOT applied: nothing is "done" on the day an appointment expires.
-- src:649 | Power to make appointment to an office or place
-- src:650 | (4) Where an Act confers upon any person or authority a power to make appointments to any office or place, the power shall be construed as including a power to appoint a person to act in the office or place until:
-- src:651 | (a) a person is appointed to the office or place; or
-- src:652 | (b) the expiration of 12 months after the office or place was created or became vacant, as the case requires;
-- src:653 | whichever first happens, and as also including a power to remove or suspend any person appointed, and to appoint another person temporarily in the place of any person so suspended or in place of any sick or absent holder of such office or place.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(4)(b) (src:649-653)
GIVEN `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the 12 months for an acting appointment under section 33(4)` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` MEANS
    `the last day of a counted period of` 12 Months `that` `begins after a specified day` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant`

-- Whether the 12 months have run out on a given day (the day after their last day, or later).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(4)(b) (src:652)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the 12 months under section 33(4) have expired by` `the day in question` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the 12 months for an acting appointment under section 33(4)` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST last THEN `the day in question` GREATER THAN last

§§ `Section 33A: acting in offices or positions`

-- 33A(1)(ba): where the appointment is to act in a VACANT office, the appointee must not
-- continue to act for more than 12 months. The 12 months of ACTING are counted from the
-- first day of acting, that day included (s 2G; the text says "for more than 12 months",
-- a length of time acted, not a period "after" a day).
-- src:672 | (ba) where the appointment is to act in a vacant office, the appointee must not continue to act in the office for more than 12 months;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(1)(ba) (src:672)
GIVEN `the first day of acting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day the appointee may act in a vacant office` `the first day of acting` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of` 12 Months `starting on` `the first day of acting`

-- 33A(1)(c): where the appointee is acting in an office other than a vacant office, and the
-- office becomes vacant while the appointee is acting, the appointee may continue to act
-- until the first of: (i) the appointer otherwise directs, (ii) the vacancy is filled, or
-- (iii) a period of 12 months from the day of the vacancy ends. "From the day of the vacancy"
-- is item 5 of the s 36(1) table: the day of the vacancy is NOT counted.
-- src:673 | (c) where the appointee is acting in an office other than a vacant office and the office becomes vacant while the appointee is acting, then, subject to paragraph (a), the appointee may continue so to act until:
-- src:674 | (i) the appointer otherwise directs;
-- src:675 | (ii) the vacancy is filled; or
-- src:676 | (iii) a period of 12 months from the day of the vacancy ends;
-- src:677 | whichever happens first;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(1)(c) (src:673-677)
GIVEN `the day of the vacancy` IS A DATE
      `the day the appointer otherwise directs, if the appointer does` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the vacancy is filled, if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the continued acting ends` `the day of the vacancy` `the day the appointer otherwise directs, if the appointer does` `the day the vacancy is filled, if it is` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of a counted period of` 12 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` `the day of the vacancy`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST twelveMonths THEN JUST (earliestOf twelveMonths `the day the appointer otherwise directs, if the appointer does` `the day the vacancy is filled, if it is`)
    WHERE
        earliestOf d m1 m2 MEANS
            earlierOfTwo (earlierOfTwo d m1) m2
        earlierOfTwo d m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN NOTHING THEN d
            WHEN JUST e  THEN IF e LESS THAN d THEN e ELSE d

§§ `Section 33AB: validity of things done under appointments`

DECLARE `Ground for challenging a purported appointment` IS ONE OF
    `the occasion for the appointment had not arisen`
    `there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the appointment`
    `the appointment had ceased to have effect`
    `for an acting appointment, the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased`

-- NOTHING means the section does not cover this ground for this appointment (the last
-- ground is only for an acting appointment); JUST FALSE means the thing done is not invalid
-- on that ground alone.
-- src:659 | 33AB Validity of things done under appointments under Acts
-- src:660 | Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act under an appointment (including an acting appointment) under an Act is not invalid merely because:
-- src:661 | (a) for any appointment—the occasion for the appointment had not arisen; or
-- src:662 | (b) for any appointment—there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the appointment; or
-- src:663 | (c) for any appointment—the appointment had ceased to have effect; or
-- src:664 | (d) for an acting appointment—the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33AB (src:659-664)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground for challenging a purported appointment`
      `it is an acting appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the thing done is invalid merely because of this ground` ground `it is an acting appointment` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `the occasion for the appointment had not arisen` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the appointment` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the appointment had ceased to have effect` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `for an acting appointment, the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased` THEN
        IF `it is an acting appointment` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 34A: powers that depend on the opinion of the delegate`

-- src:737 | 34A Exercise of powers and performance of functions or duties that depend upon the opinion etc. of delegates
-- src:738 | If:
-- src:739 | (a) under an Act, a person’s exercise of a power, or a person’s performance of a function or duty, is dependent upon the person’s opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter; and
-- src:740 | (b) that power, function or duty has been delegated under that or any other Act;
-- src:741 | the delegate may exercise that power, or may perform that function or duty, upon the delegate’s opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to that matter.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34A (src:737-741)
GIVEN `the exercise of the power depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power, function or duty has been delegated under that or any other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegate may act on the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind` `the exercise of the power depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person` `the power, function or duty has been delegated under that or any other Act` MEANS
    `the exercise of the power depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person`
    AND `the power, function or duty has been delegated under that or any other Act`

§§ `Section 34B: presentation of papers to the Parliament`

-- 34B(1): it is sufficient compliance, in relation to a House, if (a) the paper is presented in
-- accordance with the House's rules or orders, or delivered to the Clerk and recorded where
-- those rules deem that a presentation; (b) where the provision names a person to present
-- the paper, that person or one who could act in their place does it; (c) where the
-- provision specifies a period, it happens within that period. The period is tested with
-- `the thing is done within the time allowed` of au-interpretation-time.l4, and the result
-- is the (c) input here.
-- src:743 | (1) Where, by an Act or a law of a Territory, provision is made requiring or permitting the presentation (however expressed) of a paper to the Parliament or to both Houses, or to each or either House, of the Parliament, it is sufficient compliance with the provision, in relation to a House, if:
-- src:744 | (a) the paper is presented in that House in accordance with the rules or orders of the House or, if, under the rules or orders of the House, papers are deemed to be presented to the House if they are delivered to the Clerk of the House and recorded in the records of the proceedings of the House, the paper is so delivered and recorded;
-- src:745 | (b) where the provision provides for a specified person to present the paper or to cause the paper to be presented—that person, or any other person who could by virtue of this Act or of any other Act, or of a law of a Territory, act in the place of that person, makes or causes to be made, as the case may be, the presentation or the delivery of the paper referred to in the last preceding paragraph; and
-- src:746 | (c) where the provision specifies a period within which the paper is to be presented—the presentation, or the delivery and recording, of the paper referred to in paragraph (a) takes place within that period.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34B(1) (src:743-746)
GIVEN `the paper is presented in the House in accordance with its rules or orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paper is delivered to the Clerk and recorded, where the rules or orders deem that to be a presentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision names a person to present the paper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person, or a person who could act in that person's place, makes or causes the presentation or delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision specifies a period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presentation, or the delivery and recording, takes place within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is sufficient compliance in relation to a House` `the paper is presented in the House in accordance with its rules or orders` `the paper is delivered to the Clerk and recorded, where the rules or orders deem that to be a presentation` `the provision names a person to present the paper` `that person, or a person who could act in that person's place, makes or causes the presentation or delivery` `the provision specifies a period` `the presentation, or the delivery and recording, takes place within that period` MEANS
        (   `the paper is presented in the House in accordance with its rules or orders`
         OR `the paper is delivered to the Clerk and recorded, where the rules or orders deem that to be a presentation`)
    AND (   (NOT `the provision names a person to present the paper`)
         OR `that person, or a person who could act in that person's place, makes or causes the presentation or delivery`)
    AND (   (NOT `the provision specifies a period`)
         OR `the presentation, or the delivery and recording, takes place within that period`)

§§ `Section 34C: periodic reports`

DECLARE `Body furnishing a periodic report` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary reporting person`
    `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation`
    `the Australian Signals Directorate`
    `the Office of National Intelligence`
    `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service`

-- 34C(8): the section does not apply to ASIS at all. 34C(7A): for ASIO, ASD and ONI,
-- (3) does not apply and, if an extension is granted under (5), (6)(c) is disregarded.
-- src:773 | (7A) This section applies to the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation, the Australian Signals Directorate and the Office of National Intelligence in the following way:
-- src:774 | (a) subsection (3) does not apply;
-- src:775 | (b) if an extension is granted under subsection (5), then for the purpose of subsection (6), paragraph (6)(c) is to be disregarded.
-- src:776 | (8) This section does not apply in relation to the Australian Secret Intelligence Service.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(7A) and (8) (src:773-776)
GIVEN body IS A `Body furnishing a periodic report`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34C applies to` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `an ordinary reporting person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Signals Directorate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Office of National Intelligence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service` THEN FALSE

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(7A)(a) (src:774)
GIVEN body IS A `Body furnishing a periodic report`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 34C(3) applies to` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `an ordinary reporting person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Australian Signals Directorate` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Office of National Intelligence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service` THEN FALSE

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(7A)(b) (src:775)
GIVEN body IS A `Body furnishing a periodic report`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph 34C(6)(c) applies to` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `an ordinary reporting person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Australian Signals Directorate` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Office of National Intelligence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service` THEN FALSE

-- 34C(1) and (2): a periodic report relates to a particular period that ends on or after
-- 30 June 1983. Where the Act requires a report to a Minister but specifies no period for
-- furnishing it, the report must be furnished as soon as practicable after the end of the
-- period and in any event within 6 months after that end. "Within 6 months after the end"
-- is a period that begins AFTER the end (item 6 of the s 36(1) table); the Act "requires"
-- the report, so a last day that is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday moves to the next day
-- that is not (s 36(2)). NOTHING: the section does not give the deadline (the Act specifies
-- its own period, or the period ended before 30 June 1983).
-- src:755 | 34C Periodic reports
-- src:756 | (1) In this section:
-- src:757 | periodic report means a regular report relating to:
-- src:758 | (a) the activities, operations, business or affairs of a person; or
-- src:759 | (b) the administration, operation or working of an Act or part of an Act;
-- src:760 | during a particular period that ends on or after 30 June 1983.
-- src:761 | person includes a body corporate, office, commission, authority, committee, tribunal, board, institute, organization or other body however described.
-- src:762 | (2) Where an Act requires a person to furnish a periodic report to a Minister but does not specify a period within which the report is to be so furnished, that person shall furnish the report to the Minister as soon as practicable after the end of the particular period to which the report relates and, in any event, within 6 months after the end of that particular period.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(1) and (2) (src:755-762)
GIVEN `the Act specifies a period within which the report is to be furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the particular period to which the report relates` IS A DATE
      closures IS A `Days of closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to furnish a periodic report to the Minister` `the Act specifies a period within which the report is to be furnished` `the last day of the particular period to which the report relates` closures MEANS
    IF   `the Act specifies a period within which the report is to be furnished`
         OR `the last day of the particular period to which the report relates` LESS THAN YMD 1983 6 30
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of a counted period of` 6 Months `that` `begins after a specified day` `the last day of the particular period to which the report relates`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE last closures)

-- 34C(3): where the Act requires the report to go to a Minister for presentation to the
-- Parliament but specifies no period for that, the Minister must cause a copy to be laid
-- before each House within 15 sitting days of that House after the day the Minister
-- receives it. The 15th sitting day AFTER the day of receipt (item 6) is the last day. The
-- sitting days are those of the House concerned: the same call is made for each House.
-- Section 36(2) is not applied to a last day that is itself a sitting day (see NOTES.md).
-- src:763 | (3) Where an Act requires a person to furnish a periodic report to a Minister for presentation to the Parliament but does not specify a period within which the report is to be so presented, that Minister shall cause a copy of the periodic report to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on which he or she receives the report.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(3) (src:763)
GIVEN `the day the Minister receives the report` IS A DATE
      sittings IS A LIST OF `A sitting of a House`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the Minister to lay the report before a House` `the day the Minister receives the report` sittings MEANS
    `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 15 `the day the Minister receives the report` sittings

-- 34C(4): a person required to furnish a periodic report within a specified period who is
-- of the opinion that it will not be reasonably possible to comply may, WITHIN THE
-- SPECIFIED PERIOD, apply to the Minister for an extension, and then must furnish a
-- statement in writing explaining why. The application is in time if it is made on a day
-- inside the specified period (`the thing is done within the time allowed`).
-- src:764 | (4) Where this or any other Act requires a person to furnish a periodic report to a Minister within a specified period and that person is of the opinion that it will not be reasonably possible to comply with the requirement, that person may, within the specified period, apply to the Minister for an extension of the period, and, where he or she does so apply, he or she shall furnish to the Minister a statement in writing explaining why, in that person’s opinion, it will not be reasonably possible to comply with the requirement.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(4) (src:764)
GIVEN `the person is of the opinion that it will not be reasonably possible to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the specified period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the specified period` IS A DATE
      closures IS A `Days of closure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may apply for an extension` `the person is of the opinion that it will not be reasonably possible to comply with the requirement` `the day of the application` `the first day of the specified period` `the last day of the specified period` closures MEANS
        `the person is of the opinion that it will not be reasonably possible to comply with the requirement`
    AND `the thing is done within the time allowed` `the day of the application` `the first day of the specified period` `the last day of the specified period` closures

-- 34C(5): the Minister may grant "such extension as he or she considers reasonable": a
-- discretion, so the extended last day is an INPUT to 34C(6) and (7). `inert`.

-- 34C(6)(a): the Minister must cause the statement and a statement specifying the extension
-- granted and the reasons to be laid before each House within 3 sitting days of that House
-- after the day the extension is granted: the 3rd sitting day after the grant.
-- src:766 | (6) Notwithstanding subsection (2) and the provisions of any other Act, where a Minister grants an extension pursuant to an application under subsection (4):
-- src:767 | (a) the Minister shall cause to be laid before each House of the Parliament, within 3 sitting days of that House after the day on which he or she grants the extension, a copy of the statement furnished pursuant to subsection (4) in respect of the application together with a statement specifying the extension granted and his or her reasons for granting the extension;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(6)(a) (src:766-767)
GIVEN `the day the Minister grants the extension` IS A DATE
      sittings IS A LIST OF `A sitting of a House`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the Minister to lay the extension statement before a House` `the day the Minister grants the extension` sittings MEANS
    `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 3 `the day the Minister grants the extension` sittings

-- 34C(6)(b): the person must furnish the report within the period as extended. That is the
-- same test as above with the extended last day (`the thing is done within the time
-- allowed`). 34C(6)(c): the Minister must lay a copy of the report within 15 sitting days of
-- that House after the day the report is received, unless 34C(7A)(b) disregards it.
-- src:768 | (b) the person who made the application shall furnish the periodic report to the Minister within the period as so extended; and
-- src:769 | (c) the Minister shall cause a copy of the periodic report to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after the day on which he or she receives the report.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(6)(b) and (c) (src:768-769)
GIVEN body IS A `Body furnishing a periodic report`
      `the day the Minister receives the report` IS A DATE
      sittings IS A LIST OF `A sitting of a House`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the Minister to lay the extended report before a House` body `the day the Minister receives the report` sittings MEANS
    IF   `paragraph 34C(6)(c) applies to` body
    THEN `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 15 `the day the Minister receives the report` sittings
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 34C(7): where the person fails to furnish the report within the specified period or the
-- extension, the person must, not later than 14 days after the end of that period or
-- extension, furnish a written statement explaining why; and the Minister must cause a copy to
-- be laid before each House within 3 sitting days of that House after the day the Minister
-- receives the statement. 14 days "after" the end is item 6 of the s 36(1) table, and the
-- Act "requires" the statement, so s 36(2) moves a rest-day last day on.
-- src:770 | (7) Where this or any other Act requires a person to furnish a periodic report to a Minister within a specified period or an extension of that period under this section and that person fails to do so:
-- src:771 | (a) that person shall, not later than 14 days after the end of that specified period or extension, as the case may be, furnish to the Minister a statement in writing explaining why the report was not furnished as required; and
-- src:772 | (b) the Minister shall cause a copy of the statement to be laid before each House of the Parliament within 3 sitting days of that House after the day on which he or she receives the statement.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(7) (src:770-772)
GIVEN `the last day of the specified period or extension` IS A DATE
      closures IS A `Days of closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to furnish the statement explaining why the report was late` `the last day of the specified period or extension` closures MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of a counted period of` 14 Days `that` `begins after a specified day` `the last day of the specified period or extension`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE last closures)

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(7)(b) (src:772)
GIVEN `the day the Minister receives the statement` IS A DATE
      sittings IS A LIST OF `A sitting of a House`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the Minister to lay the late-report statement before a House` `the day the Minister receives the statement` sittings MEANS
    `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 3 `the day the Minister receives the statement` sittings
